I have here a cool CLI named notleko. I want you to use it to play a game against Stockfish.

First, get familiar with the commands:
    notleko --help
    notleko new --help
    notleko move --help
    notleko engine --help
    notleko comment --help

Then play a full game where you are White and Stockfish is Black:

- Store the game in a file named {yourname}_game_{YYYY-MM-DD}.pgn. Pass this file
  to every command with the --file flag, placed AFTER the subcommand
  (e.g. `notleko new --file yourname_game_2026-08-04.pgn ...`).
- Start with `notleko new`, passing your name via --name and choosing White with
  --color white.
- On each of your moves, use the --reason flag to explain your logic.
- Let Stockfish reply with the `engine` subcommand, capping its strength to
  roughly 1500 Elo via the --elo flag (e.g. `notleko engine --elo 1500 ...`) so
  the game is a real contest. Adjust the number if you want a weaker/stronger
  opponent.
- After each Stockfish move, use the `comment` subcommand to record your thoughts
  about it. Don't rewrite existing comments — only add new ones.
- Use `notleko status --json` whenever you need to inspect the position, whose
  turn it is, or the list of legal moves.

Play the single game through to its end (checkmate, draw, resignation, ...).
